import redox_ast::Expr

-- | The argument positions holding an application hole, `_` — plan 85 leaf 1.
-- |
-- | ```text
-- | String::from _      [0]
-- | compare _ _         [0, 1]
-- | .insert k _ m       [1]
-- | add 1 2             []
-- | ```
-- |
-- | Plan 56 §11.1 proved its own boundary is not movable by effort: arity is
-- | knowable **only** for a bare `Expr::Ident` naming a signature in the file
-- | being compiled, so every `Expr::Path`, every `where` local, every lambda
-- | parameter and every imported bare name is unknown-arity and emits as a
-- | call. A hole takes arity out of the question — *n* holes make an
-- | *n*-parameter closure and the callee is never consulted.
-- |
-- | It is also strictly stronger than currying rather than a workaround for it.
-- | Currying abstracts over a **suffix** of the argument list; a hole abstracts
-- | over **any** position. `.insert k _ m` — receiver supplied, key supplied,
-- | middle argument abstracted — has no prefix-based spelling at all.
-- |
-- | # `_` has four positions and this is only one of them
-- |
-- | Plan 85 leaf 1's measurement, 2026-11-11, and it corrected the plan: `_`
-- | was expected to be `RDX0101` in expression position and is **not**. It
-- | lexes as an ordinary `Expr::Ident` whose text is `"_"` and emits verbatim,
-- | so `add _ 2` already produced `add(_, 2)` — which rustc rejects with *"in
-- | expressions, `_` can only be used on the left-hand side of an
-- | assignment"*. So this row changes what a hole **means** rather than adding
-- | it.
-- |
-- | That rustc message names the one position that must not change, and the
-- | plan did not know about it: **`_ := e` is legitimate**, emitting Rust's
-- | discard assignment `_ = e;`, measured clean. It is untouched because an
-- | assignment target never reaches `emit_application`. The other two — a
-- | pattern's wildcard and a type's inferred `_` — are not expressions at all.
-- |
-- | Position decides between them, which is the rule plan 57 already
-- | established for `.`: *"a `.` in head position calls, a `.` after an
-- | expression selects a field"*. One token, four jobs, no lookahead.
export(crate) holes : &[Expr] -> Vec<usize>
holes args =
  mut found : Vec<usize> = Vec::new ()
  for pair in .enumerate (.iter args)
    is_hole = case pair.1 of
      Expr::Ident i -> i.text == "_"
      _ -> false
    if is_hole
      .push pair.0 found
  found
